e808266f-920e-42df-957b-a8c9015307c4	f434baf1-92d7-4214-9f0e-c6db6ee52069	bf65a440-d3bb-4f55-831f-636829ed74fc	Prompt: What are the main benefits of TypeScript? Answer briefly.\nAnswer: Short version — four real wins:\n\n1. **Catches bugs at compile time** — wrong types, missing props, bad calls. Not at 3am in prod.\n2. **Refactoring confidence** — rename something, TS flags every broken reference.\n3. **Better autocomplete** — the editor knows what an object *is*, not just what it's named.\n4. **Self-documenting code** — the signature tells you the contract, no reading the body.\n\nBasically: it turns "hope it works" into "know it works."	[-0.016740912571549416, 0.013733364641666412, -0.009247958660125732, 0.03383040800690651, 0.028137020766735077, -0.017073538154363632, 0.013898498378694057, 0.024787144735455513, 0.00788403581827879, 0.022659603506326675, -0.013974222354590893, -0.01569570042192936, 0.0011681214673444629, -0.02385667897760868, -0.011715932749211788, 0.011196381412446499, -0.020634854212403297, -0.009502495639026165, 0.014845638535916805, -0.037339307367801666, -0.0023898351937532425, -0.006306102499365807, 0.0013646080624312162, -0.0006808972102589905, -0.02712525986135006, 0.038380250334739685, 0.02200479991734028, 0.005942251067608595, -0.009395035915076733, 0.03236202523112297, 0.027367064729332924, -0.029162872582674026, -0.0028052981942892075, 0.0066570923663675785, -0.06431789696216583, -0.00949966348707676, 0.010893123224377632, -0.0064203981310129166, -0.008756114169955254, -0.022893352434039116, 0.005880831740796566, -0.005598844960331917, 0.002843750175088644, -0.02299949713051319, 0.009776775725185871, -0.006445779465138912, 0.025246139615774155, -0.015476798638701439, 0.018522370606660843, -0.007516658399254084, 0.029438745230436325, -0.0026341183111071587, 0.041567038744688034, -0.01435115933418274, 0.014514933340251446, 0.020076021552085876, -0.05127783864736557, -0.0016240355325862765, -0.0028249165043234825, 0.018476976081728935, -