b8f58f48-09e1-4f55-b063-f96aba7ab282	f434baf1-92d7-4214-9f0e-c6db6ee52069	cf5a2942-cfa0-4da2-9f6f-5f0bf84e4041	Prompt: What are the main benefits of TypeScript? Answer briefly.\nAnswer: TypeScript's main wins, briefly:\n\n- **Compile-time errors** — catches type mismatches and null bugs before runtime.\n- **Refactoring safety** — rename or restructure and the compiler flags every broken call site.\n- **Better tooling** — autocomplete and navigation that actually understand your code.\n- **Self-documenting types** — the signature is the contract, no wiki needed.\n- **JS compatibility** — runs on top of JavaScript, adopt it file by file.\n\nTrade-off: extra setup and typing up front.	[-0.02260182797908783, 0.008276758715510368, -0.012026596814393997, 0.026377970352768898, 0.017977679148316383, -0.013696372509002686, 0.013149745762348175, 0.022295575588941574, 0.011373247019946575, 0.025414586067199707, -0.004710814915597439, -0.022665202617645264, -0.009572489187121391, -0.01703319326043129, -0.03144308179616928, 0.0017978668911382556, -0.01285806205123663, 0.0008488113526254892, -0.001621431321837008, -0.03753044083714485, 0.0038142253179103136, -0.009342740289866924, 0.013011246919631958, -0.01563328690826893, -0.03991321474313736, 0.03404758498072624, 0.02499379776418209, -0.00849829614162445, -0.012993605807423592, 0.04445987194776535, 0.038632217794656754, -0.014329792931675911, -0.006427471060305834, 0.003155226120725274, -0.06140466034412384, -0.020659776404500008, 0.011705901473760605, -0.010247841477394104, -0.0036320462822914124, -0.006297564134001732, -0.00579199381172657, 0.007158024236559868, -0.02267865091562271, -0.02232380397617817, 0.009694675914943218, -0.012269483879208565, 0.026156557723879814, -0.015871677547693253, 0.020868511870503426, 0.00541657255962491, 0.04100536182522774, -0.008024203591048717, 0.044647861272096634, -0.022720923647284508, 0.016987673938274384, 0.0063297138549387455, -0.05416928976774216, 0.0011211499804630876, -0.0077885584