5cf4467b-4b1b-429e-98fa-4e2a5bc93545	tg:495185511	assistant	Here's a clean Python function that calculates the factorial of a non-negative integer:\n\n```python\ndef factorial(n):\n    """Return the factorial of n. Raises ValueError for negative input."""\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError("Input must be an integer")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError("Factorial is not defined for negative numbers")\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        return 1\n    result = 1\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        result *= i\n    return result\n\n# Test examples\nprint(factorial(5))   # 120\nprint(factorial(0))   # 1\nprint(factorial(7))   # 5040\n```\n\nYou can also use recursion or `math.factorial` from the standard library if preferred.	{}	2026-06-25 11:29:48.028173+00
